  "reason": "The strongest result so far is config_002 (rna_only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, avgpool) at 0.6501 acc, a massive jump over its singleprofile counterpart config_011 (0.5203). This establishes multiprofile + avgpool as the dominant design axis. The critical open question is whether avgpool is the optimal aggregation or whether a transformer-based aggregation can further improve multiprofile performance. config_013 (rna_only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, transformer) is a clean single-variable comparison against config_002, isolating the aggregation mechanism while holding model setting, profile setting, and RNA encoder constant. The answer directly determines which aggregation to pair with any future multimodal multiprofile experiments, making it the highest-information experiment under the limited budget. If transformer outperforms avgpool, it signals a richer profile-level interaction model; if avgpool holds or wins, it confirms the simpler strategy and redirects exploration toward other variables (e.g., adding image, changing encoder)."
